@.str.209 = private unnamed_addr constant [970 x i8] c"Returns a new mesh with the faces selected by a boolean mask.\0A\0AArgs:\0A    mask (open3d.core.Tensor): A boolean mask with the shape (N) with N as the\0A        number of faces in the mesh.\0A\0AReturns:\0A    A new mesh with the selected faces. If the original mesh is empty, return an empty mesh.\0A\0AExample:\0A\0A    This code partitions the mesh using PCA and then visualized the individual\0A    parts::\0A\0A        import open3d as o3d\0A        import numpy as np\0A        bunny = o3d.data.BunnyMesh()\0A        mesh = o3d.t.geometry.TriangleMesh.from_legacy(o3d.io.read_triangle_mesh(bunny.path))\0A        num_partitions = mesh.pca_partition(max_faces=20000)\0A\0A        parts = []\0A        for i in range(num_partitions):\0A            mask = mesh.triangle.partition_ids == i\0A            part = mesh.select_faces_by_mask(mask)\0A            part.vertex.colors = np.tile(np.random.rand(3), (part.vertex.positions.shape[0],1))\0A            parts.append(part)\0A\0A        o3d.visualization.draw(parts)\0A\0A\00", align 1
